PATCH 168: the resource-list walk cursor+walker FUN_0000_c157/c164 (asm 0xc157/0xc164) on the
mission-setup path (e006-tail -> d755 -> c164).  c157 inits the cursor a29e = the table base
near-offset DGROUP:0xdfbc + count a2a0 = 0xb6; c164 walks the stride-4 table returning each
nonzero entry (found near-offset in AX, CF via g_fist_cf).  Ghidra typed a29e int*/undefined2*
so c157 stored a 4-byte host pointer and c164 dereferenced the near-offset as a host ptr ->
the SIGSEGV at FUN_0000_c164 (`while(*piVar1==0)`, fault = the near-offset 0x20fc; chain
d755->c164).  Rebased both through g_mem+0x1c000 as 16-bit DGROUP near-offsets; c164 now returns
the found si in AX and its x86 CF via the shim g_fist_cf (consumed by d755, patch 169).  The
walk logic is instruction-faithful (asm 0xc157..0xc181).  Behaviour-neutral for verify
(mission-setup path, unreached by the 19 flows).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -1240,7 +1240,7 @@
